" :question/problem "![](images/62/62bc017c2a920b6e1014fe652ce847d76b062bf2290e2916a99b830e8e10db45.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate the value of $2÷\\frac{3}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate $2÷\\frac{3}{5}$, we first need to divide each of the $2$ wholes into $5$ equal parts.\n\n![](images/18/18252aca223fa7861bd1c55b53514853bb0ecb5584742ad6f6c127b71791188d.png)\n\n \n\nNext, we break this into groups of $3$:\n\n![](images/18/18af0e24ce19e818f9b3ec3189db0e4edecbf06789667dbe3cfa97173ba69996.png)\n\n \n\nNote the following: \n\n- We got $\\boxed{\\text{3}}$ full groups.\n\n- There is $1$ piece left over out of a possible group of $3.$ So the fractional part of our answer is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{3}{5}=\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\,\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bc04b3fe-ba9f-5ce5-875b-438fcbdf87f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bc04b3fe-ba9f-5ce5-875b-438fcbdf87f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc04b3fe-ba9f-5ce5-875b-438fcbdf87f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0adb188f-a662-527d-866b-95e2f2aa5ebf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-85a62a0a-61b9-5d9a-85c1-85fbb9dccb00" "answer-76574c4c-211c-5afd-b4a0-58983afe1ac5" "answer-5939f342-df6d-5651-a330-f13e59fef835" "answer-0adb188f-a662-527d-866b-95e2f2aa5ebf" "answer-e0fbd55c-d332-5dfa-9479-ed443a63cada"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85a62a0a-61b9-5d9a-85c1-85fbb9dccb00" :answer/id #uuid "85a62a0a-61b9-5d9a-85c1-85fbb9dccb00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76574c4c-211c-5afd-b4a0-58983afe1ac5" :answer/id #uuid "76574c4c-211c-5afd-b4a0-58983afe1ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5939f342-df6d-5651-a330-f13e59fef835" :answer/id #uuid "5939f342-df6d-5651-a330-f13e59fef835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0adb188f-a662-527d-866b-95e2f2aa5ebf" :answer/id #uuid "0adb188f-a662-527d-866b-95e2f2aa5ebf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0fbd55c-d332-5dfa-9479-ed443a63cada" :answer/id #uuid "e0fbd55c-d332-5dfa-9479-ed443a63cada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-68cff8ab-d96c-583e-af11-a7fb638626de" :question/id #uuid "68cff8ab-d96c-583e-af11-a7fb638626de" :question/math-academy-id "q-237502" :question/problem "![](images/38/38a8f6963fbe538fc67310e583271d8feeef3b86ec9f1e81354f179fe727963f.png)\n\nIf the model above represents $1$ whole, use the model to solve the following division problem. Express your answer as a mixed number in its simplest form.\n\n$1÷\\frac{3}{8}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To calculate $1÷\\frac{3}{8}$, we first need to divide the whole into $8$ equal parts.\n\n![](images/e5/e5c3ad39f7ebf8bb6585dfa65054bb6b0eba881f1e9f7404ae5275f5c45f3771.png)\n\n \n\nNext, we break this into groups of $3$:\n\n![](images/db/dbfd34916dd6db9467988b6b72052f9b077e4de67e2b54b9a092d959233ccc85.png)\n\n \n\nNote the following: \n\n- We got $\\boxed{\\text{2}}$ full groups.\n\n- There are $2$ parts left over out of a possible group of $3.$ So the fractional part of our answer is \n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n1÷\\frac{3}{8}=\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\,\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d49da477-d2e1-5a9b-a735-9358b5cfe076"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d49da477-d2e1-5a9b-a735-9358b5cfe076" :answer-field/id #uuid "d49da477-d2e1-5a9b-a735-9358b5cfe076" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2da6fd7c-ffd0-53f2-8b2f-b491b76fdb4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2da6fd7c-ffd0-53f2-8b2f-b491b76fdb4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2da6fd7c-ffd0-53f2-8b2f-b491b76fdb4e" :answer/id #uuid "2da6fd7c-ffd0-53f2-8b2f-b491b76fdb4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205225 :tutorial/content "When we divide a whole number by a non-unit fraction, the answer is often not a whole number. \n\nIn this lesson, we'll learn how to solve division problems in these cases using models. The process is similar to cases when the answer is a whole number (we saw this in a previous lesson). The difference now is that we have to deal with a remainder. \n\nTo demonstrate, let's use a model to solve the following division problem:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{1}} \\div \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nWe start with a model that represents $\\color{blue}1$ whole:\n\n![](images/bf/bf3da76c75a78c8f2fd64f0ad08a7de339734de12a927d164e7b0b85be5c8bca.png)\n\n \n\nWe need to determine how many times $\\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{2}}3$ fits into $\\color{blue}1$ whole. So, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split our whole into *thirds* (the denominator of our fraction):\n\n![](images/bf/bfebfebd8b72bbfe256f4cecadaa0b264be7640117b915aa574a485a0091ab09.png)\n\n- Next, we break this into groups of $\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{2}$:\n\n![](images/ac/ac3eaf757cee480d078152c974e98c9c9470cb0bb4f1ac36aefc973c40edfaef.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- We have $\\fbox{1}$ full group. This is the whole number part of our answer.\n\n- We see that there is $\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{1}$ piece left over out of a possible group of $\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{2}.$ So, the fractional part of our answer is \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{1}}{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our division problem is as follows:\n\n$$\n1 \\div \\dfrac{2}{3} = \\fbox{1} \\, \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{1}}{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{2}}\n$$\n\nLet's see another example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204108 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
